<title>FRANCE: Thomson-CSF unit wins 60 mln stg UK deal.</title>
<headline>Thomson-CSF unit wins 60 mln stg UK deal.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>French defence electronics firm Thomson-CSF said on Friday its Thomson Training &amp; Simulation unit has won a 60 million stg contract to supply training systems for Britain's Nimrod 2000 maritime patrol aircraft.</p>
<p>British Aerospace Plc, which leads the Nimrod 2000 programme, has chosen Thomson as prime contractor for supply of simulation and training equipment over the next eight years.</p>
<p>The simulators will be made in the Crawley facility, south of London. First deliveries will begin between December 2000 and June 2001 to the Royal Air Force Kinloss base in Scotland. The last systems will be delivered by 2004.</p>
</text>
